  "notes": [
    "W2 (design 1.8): lightningcss attests no cascade, so a var() or animation-name pair is graded as a name reference: kept when its name is a custom property or @keyframes rule defined in the file or its @import closure, every other pair out of both sides, counted",
    "file_edge_precision and file_edge_recall measured against an import dump's (file, imported file) pairs, there being no SCIP index: the truth is what each file's import statements name, not the files its references reach as a SCIP index's cross-file edges are, so a file reached without an import of its own (a file another one required, an autoloaded constant) is outside the truth and a resolved edge to it counts against precision, while a file imported and never referenced is in it (LB-F57)",
    "gitea: 1247 oracle and 1247 fathom name pairs name nothing defined in their file's @import closure (W2), out of both",
    "import_resolution: 88 of 88 in-repo imports resolve to a file the oracle names (0 unresolved, 0 only to other files; L3 bar: excellent \u003e= 0.95, good \u003e= 0.85); import edges precision 1 (88 of 88) and recall 1 (88 of 88); 0 of 90 imports resolved where the oracle names no file of the subject; 0 oracle imports on no statement fathom extracted; 0 oracle import targets outside the files measured",
    "normalize.css: lightningcss resolves none of fathom's imports to a file of the subject, so import_resolution has no denominator here",
    "per-file times exclude the one-time grammar compile (an untimed warm-up extraction precedes timing)",
    "pico: 118 oracle and 118 fathom name pairs name nothing defined in their file's @import closure (W2), out of both",
